//! # Closed-loop AI improvement (ARC-10 / §5.1)
//!
//! The AI system being improved is a neural surrogate ([`simorph_learning::Mlp`])
//! of a SIMORPH simulator.  The loop only uses knowledge produced by SIMORPH's
//! own *validated* simulations, and the judge is a sealed suite that the loop
//! cannot modify:
//!
//! 1. sealed held-out suite generated by the validated simulator ([`suite`]);
//! 2. initial evaluation and limit identification on a separate probe set
//!    (error map over a partition of the input space, error by physical regime);
//! 3. hypothesis ("error concentrates in cells C because data are sparse there");
//! 4. targeted Latin-hypercube design inside the worst cells;
//! 5. execution through `simorph_experiment::run_experiment`;
//! 6. independent validation of every sample (manifest invariants, reference
//!    cases, physical bounds) — rejected samples are excluded and counted;
//! 7. validated dataset with SHA-256 and provenance;
//! 8. controlled training (fixed architecture, budget and seed);
//! 9. re-evaluation on the same sealed suite;
//! 10. acceptance only on a significant paired improvement (bootstrap CI)
//!     with no regression of protected metrics; otherwise rejection;
//! 11. rollback; 12. iteration until no significant gain or budget exhausted.
//!
//! Controls ([`campaign::Variant`]): corrupted data (unit bug) must be rejected,
//! attempts to modify the sealed suite are refused, and targeted sampling is
//! compared with uniform sampling of the same size.

